Spawn, objective 217 [recoverability] (owner t489u, candidate A step 3, the second half of 216's split, sync/obj-216/scope.md; the lead's scope YES of 2026-11-18 with three conditions, sync/obj-217/scope.md; author rev-i; readers rev-j first, rev-k second): the fleet's notes folder, which 216 puts into each bundle, restored from the bundle chain and compared with the folder, read only.

Base: live main fc78b4da (216's fleet landing, live since 2026-11-18 09:41).

The problem: since 216, /var/tmp/spawn/sync (about 210 MB, 12,322 files) goes into the daily encrypted bundle: a full each week, then increments. Nothing proves it comes back. 4/216's verify owes "its bundle holds the notes folder" (sync/verify/4-216-rev-i.md, (b)).

Read first:
- crates/spawn-cli/src/backup/sync_dir.rs: what each bundle holds. sync/manifest.json lists EVERY file of the folder (path, size, mtime_ms, mode, sha256), plus taken, removed, skipped and changed_during_read. sync/files/ holds the taken files. The record's sync part is {dir, kind, base_manifest, files, bytes, taken, taken_bytes, removed, skipped, changed_during_read, manifest_sha256, scan}, or {dir, refused}.
- crates/spawn-cli/src/backup/restore_drill.rs: --only transcripts (objective 200): the chain, the key rules, the pipe (gpg into a pipe, the stream hashed, tar -t whose sha256 must be the record's, then tar -x of names chosen from that listing), fetch_members and members_of, plain_tree, the floor, DrillDir, Report and outcomes, record_verdicts.
- crates/spawn-postgres/sql/schema.sql: spawn_backup_record and the record allowlists naming backup.drilled.*; crates/spawn-postgres/src/control_mask.rs LIMITED.

What changes:
(1) `spawn backup restore-drill --only sync` drills the notes folder alone. It uses the same chain (the newest stored bundle back to its full), key rules and pipe as --only transcripts. From each link it extracts by name only manifest.json, sync/manifest.json and the files under sync/files/: no directory, no empty, `.` or `..` part, no name tar had to quote. It never extracts a transcript slice or a repository bundle. It says one line: "--only sync: the fleet's notes folder alone, ...".
(2) Restore into the drill's own folder, under sync/.
  - The newest record must hold a part. A record with no sync is a backup that cannot be restored ("the newest bundle (event N) holds no notes folder ..."). So is one whose part was dropped ("... dropped its notes folder: <the refused reason>").
  - Each link with a part: its sync/manifest.json must have the sha256 its record names (sync.manifest_sha256), else it cannot be restored. A link with no part, or a dropped one, holds no file.
  - Each file of the newest manifest comes from the newest link whose `taken` names it. A file no link holds, or one restored at another size or sha256 than the newest manifest's, cannot be restored.
  - Its line: "the notes folder: <n> file(s), <bytes> bytes, restored from <k> bundle(s) of the chain, each the newest manifest's sha256".
(3) Then the folder the newest record names (sync.dir) is compared with the restored one, read only: it is never written to, created in or removed from. Its regular files are walked; a symbolic link is never followed. For each file of the newest manifest:
  - live has the same sha256: the same;
  - live has other bytes and an mtime at or after the newest bundle's start (its manifest.json's created_at_ms): changed since (expected). A file the bundle read was read at or after its start, so any write since gives it such an mtime;
  - live has other bytes and an earlier mtime: a mismatch (the backup holds older bytes than the folder had when the bundle began);
  - no longer in live: removed since (expected), one gone while the drill reads it included (its lstat or its bytes answer not found);
  - unreadable: a mismatch.
  For each live file the manifest lacks:
  - listed in the newest manifest's skipped or changed_during_read: said apart;
  - else written at or after the newest bundle's start (its manifest.json's created_at_ms): made since (expected);
  - else a mismatch (the backup lacks a file older than it).
  A folder that cannot be read is one mismatch naming it. Its line: "the notes folder against live <dir>: <a> the same, <b> changed since, <c> removed since, <d> made since, <e> skipped or changed while bundled, <m> mismatch(es)".
(4) Exit 0 with no mismatch, 1 with any or when it cannot be restored, 2 when it cannot run, as the other drills. Each mismatch goes on stderr as "restore-drill: mismatch: sync/<path>: ...", the first NAMED of them.
  - It records backup.drilled.sync alone, exactly {type, ok, reason, bundle, bundle_event_id, mismatches, duration_ms}, as backup.drilled.transcripts. It writes no transcripts or missions record.
  - schema.sql: backup.drilled.sync joins the log's backup kinds, spawn_backup_record's type list, the fixed-shape drill check and the ok/reason/bundle checks.
  - control_mask LIMITED: ("backup.drilled.sync", "reason").
(5) Its drill folder:
  - Made under --into, else /data/tmp, as the others'.
  - Never under the notes folder: --into under it is refused, exit 2, nothing recorded.
  - Holds only directories and regular files (plain_only), and is removed as the transcripts drill's is.
  - The floor (SPAWN_BACKUP_DRILL_FLOOR_MB) counts each link's stored_bytes and sync.taken_bytes plus the newest record's sync.bytes.
(6) Owner:
  - deploy/systemd/spawn-backup-restore-drill-sync.service runs `spawn backup restore-drill --only sync` with the bundle's environment, after spawn-backup-bundle.service.
  - Its .timer runs daily at 06:30. It ships disabled; the lead enables it after one supervised run on live.
  - deploy/backup/README.md gets the drill's paragraph and its schedule entry, saying so.
  - The Core lines recovery row is the lead's, after that run, and is not in 217.

What stays as it is: the bundle and 216's part; every other drill mode, their records and their output; restore-drill with no --only.

Files: crates/spawn-cli/src/backup/restore_drill.rs (the --only sync wiring, Report.sync, the third outcome, the floor's bytes, docs), crates/spawn-cli/src/backup/restore_drill/sync.rs (new, with its unit tests), crates/spawn-postgres/sql/schema.sql, crates/spawn-postgres/src/control_mask.rs, crates/spawn-postgres/tests/backup.rs (a new store test); owner: deploy/systemd/spawn-backup-restore-drill-sync.{service,timer}, deploy/backup/README.md, rsi/scenarios/217.sh, rsi/backlog/217.json.

Acceptance: rsi/scenarios/217.sh. It is black box on its own database, scratch HOME and GNUPGHOME, against 104's R2 stand-in (216.sh's world), with two real `spawn backup bundle` runs over a made-up notes folder: a full, then an increment after an append, an add and a remove. The drill is given --into a scratch parent. Its header lists (1)-(10), (5b), (5c), (5d), (8b) and (9b):
- (2) the drill passes, restores every file, finds all the same, and records one backup.drilled.sync {ok true, the newest bundle's key and event} and no other drill record; nothing is left in the parent;
- (3) --keep's folder holds every file of the folder byte for byte, a full-only file included, and no transcript or repository bundle;
- (4) an append, an add and a remove after the bundle pass: "1 changed since, 1 removed since, 1 made since";
- (5) other bytes with the bundled mtime put back, other bytes with an mtime between the bundled one and the bundle's start, and an old file the backup lacks: exit 1, 3 mismatches named, the record ok false;
- (5b) the notes folder gone for one run: exit 1, one mismatch naming it;
- (5c) a live file made unreadable for one run: exit 1, one mismatch naming it;
- (5d) the bundled symbolic link (in the manifest's skipped) replaced live by a regular file written a day before the bundle: passes, "1 skipped or changed while bundled", no mismatch;
- (6) the newest link's object replaced by another ciphertext: cannot be restored, exit 1;
- (7) the unit, run as systemd runs it with --into, passes; the timer names an OnCalendar;
- (8) --into under the notes folder: exit 2, nothing recorded;
- (8b) a floor no disk meets: exit 2, the floor named, nothing recorded or made;
- (9) a newest bundle whose part was dropped: exit 1, its reason named;
- (9b) a newest bundle made with no notes folder set: exit 1, its reason saying it holds no notes folder;
- (10) every drill leaves the notes folder exactly as it was (path, type, size, mode, mtime, sha256), and no secret or file content is in any output or record.
On live main fc78b4da, and on live main 08c8138b (the proof's), 217.sh exits 1.

Tests (unit, restore_drill/sync.rs): each file from the newest link that took it, and said apart the newest manifest's skipped and changed_during_read (not an older link's); a path no link took, a manifest not the record's sha256, a newest record with no part or a dropped one; the comparison by bytes then by the bundle's start (same, changed since, a mismatch with the mtime set back and one written between the bundled copy and the start, removed, made since, apart, an older file the manifest lacks, a folder that cannot be read, a live file that cannot be read, a file removed during the read of live: left out of the listing, or removed since when its bytes are gone); a taken file whose bytes are not the newest manifest's; the listing takes the notes part alone; the floor's bytes. Store (tests/backup.rs): backup.drilled.sync accepted in the drill shape and refused outside it. No test is renamed or dropped.

Not in 217: the Core lines row (the lead's); 216's next-change notes (rev-j n1-n4, rev-k n1-n2; bundle side, a separate follow-up).

